            "section_id": "doc-repatha-not-made-with-natural-rubber-latex-prescribing-information-section-12-1",
            "section_kind": "fullPrescribingInformation",
            "section_title": "12.1 \nMechanism of Action  ",
            "source_spans": "[{\"archive_block_id\":\"doc-repatha-not-made-with-natural-rubber-latex-prescribing-information-page-0010-text\",\"block_end\":443,\"block_start\":0,\"end\":899,\"page\":10,\"source_block_id\":\"doc-repatha-not-made-with-natural-rubber-latex-prescribing-information-section-12-1-p0010\",\"start\":456}]",
            "source_text": "12.1 \nMechanism of Action  \n \nEvolocumab is a human monoclonal IgG2 directed against human proprotein convertase subtilisin kexin \ntype 9 (PCSK9). PCSK9 binds to the low-density lipoprotein receptor (LDLR) on the surface of \nhepatocytes to promote LDLR degradation within the liver. By inhibiting the binding of PCSK9 to \nLDLR, evolocumab increases the number of LDLRs available to clear LDL from the blood, thereby \nlowering LDL-C levels. \n \n",
            "source_variant_hint": "repatha_not_made_with_natural_rubber_latex_prescribing_information.pdf",
            "token_count_is_exact": false,
            "token_count_method": "utf8-byte-upper-bound+8-reserve",
