      "question": "How does this medicine work?",
      "seconds": 7.27,
      "response": {
        "answer": "Tezepelumab-ekko binds to TSLP and stops it from attaching to its receptor. TSLP is a signal involved early in the chain of inflammation. [1]\n\nBlocking TSLP lowers markers and signals linked to inflammation. However, exactly how tezepelumab-ekko works in asthma and CRSwNP has not been firmly established. [2]",
